To force the transitions to register inside the hardware memory buffer, implement these mechanical adjustments:
Tie the Ground Planes (Mandatory): Run a dedicated wire from a large ground shield on the keyboard PCB (such as the outer frame of the micro-USB/Type-C charging port or the negative battery trace) straight to Header Pin 25 (GND) on the Banana Pi. This locks their logic definitions together.
Test an Alternative 5V Tolerant Bank (Port A): The pinctrl input structures on the Allwinner H2+ vary slightly between functional banks. Port A features slightly more sensitive Schmitt-trigger inputs than the SPI blocks on Port C.
