Use code with caution.
(If you find a line reading console=ttyS0,115200, you can safely delete that specific parameter phrase, save the file, and compile it back down to the system using sudo mkimage -C none -A arm -T script -d /boot/boot.cmd /boot/boot.scr if your Armbian build uses a compiled boot script structure). 
Step 3: Power Cycle and Listen via ttyS0
Execute a clean system reset to free the hardware tracking registers:
