This behavior explains the entire system design. The fact that 1.5 Mbps (1500000 baud) registers raw data for the touchpad but drops characters on lower baud rates is the exact technical signature of how dual-function HID peripherals handle asynchronous packets.
The keyboard and touchpad are not streaming data frames simultaneously over a unified single-wire bus. Instead, the custom clone chip dynamically alters its transmission speed depending on the specific operational subsystem you interact with:
1. The Dual-Baud Speed Selection Matrix
To handle the distinct data density requirements of a tracking pad versus a simple key layout, the matrix chip switches gears:
The Touchpad Domain (1.5 Mbps / High-Speed Burst): A touchpad tracks continuous coordinate streams (


