The Keyboard Domain (Standard Lower Speed): Keypresses only occur as discrete events. To ensure transmission reliability over a single-layer PCB, the controller drops the transmission rate significantly down to a standard sub-variant frequency when executing a keystroke.
When you configure your receiver to a flat 115200 baud, you capture the exact inverse: the keyboard transmissions resolve into garbled strings (п@) while the high-speed touchpad bursts fall outside the sampling window completely.
